<ProjectLayout slug="arena-waves">
  <p>
    When did a witch become a witch?
Even before someone called her one,
she must have already been there.
  </p>

  <p>
   People give names to what they cannot understand.
Perhaps because once something has a name,
it becomes a little less frightening.
  </p>

  <p>
    Across different lands,
she was called by different names,
and strangely, fire appeared again and again.
  </p>

  <p>
    Fire erased many things,
but it could not burn everything.
  </p>

  <p>
    Some became smoke,
some became stories,
and some remained within the body.
  </p>

    <p>
   She remembers them,
knows how to put them to sleep,
and sometimes, how to wake them.
  </p>

    <p>
   What she is capable of
is still unknown.
  </p>

    <p>
    Things that have outlived fire
rarely reveal their secrets.
  </p>


